      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Daniel Philip Meuser [ 1 ] [ 2 ] ( / \u02c8 m j u\u02d0 z \u0259r / MEW -z\u0259r ; born February 10, 1964) [ 3 ] is an American businessman and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Pennsylvania's 9th congressional district since 2019. [ 4 ] A Republican , he previously served as the secretary of revenue in the cabinet of Pennsylvania governor Tom Corbett . He was previously president of the Pride Corporation, a manufacturer of motorized wheelchairs in the Wilkes-Barre/Scranton metro area of Pennsylvania , and currently serves the company as a board member and consultant. [ 5 ] ",
